hypothesis: >-
  Lineage A / E1 (H15, H16). A phase-separated library pipeline needs no tcgen05 code: custom depthwise conv, cuBLASLt
  fp16 GEMMs, custom GELU/GRN. LayerNorm is folded away (W1' = W1*lnw, with u[k] and cst[k] computed on the side) so the
  conv needs no per-token all-channel tile. 5 launches (6 on small images) should land S rows at 25-35 us.
  Result: 16/16 pass, run_tests projects 0.594 (anchor 0.304), but S rows are 35-55 us and 7x7 rows 57-89 us. cuBLASLt
  and the fp16 hidden round trip are cheap; each custom launch costs 6-17 us, not 2 us.
expected_effect:
  S: {pct: -54, confidence: high}
  M: {pct: -68, confidence: high}
  L: {pct: -82, confidence: high}
