  - "launch floor on this B200: an empty-ish 1-block kernel measures 2.4 us under harness timing; but every custom launch here costs 6-17 us because each is a chain of 2-3 dependent global round trips plus a ramp. The lineage assumption '2 us per launch' is wrong by 3-5x; the 5-launch fixed floor is ~35-40 us at S, not ~12 [probe_b200]"
  - "cold dependent-load latency is 0.44 us per step (chain of 8 = 5.5 us, 1 = 2.4 us); a round of loads costs ~1 us once the SM is loaded [probe_b200]"
  - "K1 staging dominates the conv: removing the global->smem staging cut K1 from 20.7 to 6.5 us (1,96,56,56) and 148 to 28 us (8,320,32,32); plain LDG+STS staging (no cp.async) was equal (23 vs 20 us), so the cost is not the LDGSTS instruction. A 64-channel 7-row stage-only kernel took 9.5 us vs 5.9 us for a contiguous float4 read of the same bytes vs 1.9 us floor, i.e. about 8 GB/s per SM through LDG/LDGSTS. Total staged bytes (halo redundancy 5-13x) spread over all SMs is what matters, hence 1-warp CTAs and tall tiles in v3 [probe_b200]"
  - "dead end: same-address float4 atomics from 784 blocks into 384 sums cost K2 21 us at 1,96,56,56; fixed with 4 accumulator copies and at most 48*NC token blocks per image [probe_b200, run_tests]"
  - "cuBLASLt returns 8 heuristic algos for all 16 shapes; top-3 totals are equal within 0.3% at 1,192,28,28 (40.9/41.0/41.0 us), so algo choice is not a lever; the second probe crashed on a later CL-shape algo (illegal launch), not investigated [probe_b200]"
  - "dead end: NCHW strided-batched GEMM2 (m=HW) is slow for HW=49/196/odd and for stride-0 batch: 20-200 us (v1: 8,384,14,14 29.5 us, 2,768,7,7 24 us, 8,768 69 us, 16,768 126 us, 32,768 201 us). Channels-last GEMM2 (m=C) + a 32x32 transpose-add kernel (4-8 us) replaces it for HW<256 or HW%8!=0 [probe_b200]"
  - "TF32 (fp32 operands, torch allow_tf32) vs fp16, cold, us: 784x192x768 5.4/3.3; 784x768x192 6.2/4.3; 98x768x3072 7.3/5.2; 98x3072x768 11.8/7.2; 1568x768x3072 20.2/9.6; 8192x320x1280 19.1/9.7; 8192x1280x320 22.1/11.4; 131072x128x512 57.1/31.4; 802816x96x384 270/129. TF32 avoids the 4.7-14 MB weight conversion but is 1.4-2.1x slower; it only helps if the conversion cannot be overlapped [probe_b200]"
  - "H16: write then read a fp16 scratch after the 2xL2 zero-fill (two launches), us: 0.01 MB 5.4, 20 MB 9.0, 42 MB 14.6, 134 MB 57.4 (ideal at 7 TB/s 5.7/12/38). The hidden round trip costs ~3.6 us over the two-launch floor at 20 MB (the size of the 8,320,32,32 hidden), well under the 10 us refutation bar, and about 1.4x ideal at 134 MB: the materialised fp16 hidden is cheap [probe_b200]"
  - "precision: folding LayerNorm into the GEMM (fp16 d, fp32 partial stats, z = rstd*(Y - mean*u) + cst) and fp16 hidden with b2' as hi/lo fp16 columns passed 16/16 x 10 rounds; per-size max error was not logged by run_tests [run_tests]"
  - "residual weaknesses by launch: K2 reaches 447 us for the 616 MB hidden at the largest size (ideal ~175) and 113 us at 32,128,64,64 (ideal ~40); K1 is 954 us at the largest; K3 costs 6-17 us at every small row because it is a 3-round chain (sumsq, sqrt-reduce, W2 rows). Fusing K2+K3 work into the neighbouring GEMM (custom epilogue) or a TMA-fed conv would remove ~20 us at S [probe_b200]"
